meta {
  name: List my tastings
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/me/produce/tastings?year={{year}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  year: {{year}}
}

docs {
  What the caller has eaten in one calendar year, for the produce tracker.

  Owner-only, with no public mirror: the log is private. Never cached, so there is
  no cache tag to pair with the writes. Needs an account and nothing else: a caller
  with no game library profile gets 200, not 403.

  Slugs are the produce catalog's (src/lib/produce/catalog.ts) but are not checked
  against it, so a retired slug can still come back here. The client ignores slugs
  it does not know.

  - 200 `[{ slug, year, eatenOn }]`, eatenOn as YYYY-MM-DD, ordered by slug
  - 401 no or invalid token
  - 422 year missing or before 2020
}
